---
/**
 * S-3 · What you get — the first half of the Page IA's
 * "what-you-get / how-it-works / what-to-expect" module (Stage C).
 *
 * Responsibility (`SERVICE_PAGE_IA.md` S-3): "**reduce uncertainty by making the
 * service tangible** — and set realistic expectations." Components
 * (`SERVICE_WIREFRAME.md` S-3): "Section Header · Rich Text (deliverables ·
 * process · what to expect)."
 *
 * Spatial composition, transcribed: "the concrete substance of the service,
 * presented plainly and specifically — **practical over promotional**."
 *
 * ── ONE LIST, NOT SIX ILLUSTRATED CARDS ───────────────────────────────────
 * The approved HiFi renders deliverables as six editorial objects, each with a
 * hand-drawn SVG preview and a format badge — `.E57 / .RCP`, `.TIFF geo`,
 * `.DWG / .PDF`, `.IFC / .RVT`, `web / .E57`, `.PDF`. `Service.deliverables` is
 * `Localized<readonly string[]>`: one authored string per deliverable, with no
 * format field, no description field and no per-item illustration. §5.3 rebuilds
 * markup "from the Content Model, never from HiFi markup"; inventing three
 * sub-fields so the page can look like the prototype is exactly the field
 * invention this workstream must not do, and hard-coding six laser-scanning
 * diagrams into a generic Service page would make it Scanare 3D's page forever.
 *
 * What survives is the *composition*: a set of evenly weighted objects on a
 * ruled grid, each one deliverable, in the authored order. What is absent is the
 * per-item artwork and the format badge. Both are reported as content-model
 * gaps; if the owner wants them, they are two additive fields on the Service and
 * one element each here.
 *
 * The list is ordered because the authoring order is editorial — the owner
 * decides which deliverable a client reads first — so `<ol>` states that, and
 * the CSS suppresses the numerals the HiFi's grid does not show.
 */
import { localize } from '../../lib/content';
import type { Locale, Service } from '../../lib/content';
import type { ServiceMessages } from '../../lib/i18n/service';

interface Props {
  service: Service;
  locale: Locale;
  copy: ServiceMessages;
}

const { service, locale, copy } = Astro.props;

/* The module only renders when this is non-empty (`modules.ts`), so the
   fallback is a type guard rather than an expected state. */
const deliverables = localize(service.deliverables, locale) ?? [];
---

<div class="sv-deliverables">
  <ol class="sv-objs" aria-label={copy.deliverables.listLabel}>
    {
      deliverables.map((deliverable, index) => (
        <li class="sv-obj rv" data-rv="meta">
          <span class="sv-obj-no mono" aria-hidden="true">
            {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
          </span>
          <span class="sv-obj-name">{deliverable}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</div>
